Fix in-build SEO validator gate (task #896)

Root cause: the base index.html shipped a 251-char meta description, a
canonical, hreflang, og:*, twitter:*, keywords, robots tags and JSON-LD
with @types (SoftwareApplication, ContactPoint, EntryPoint) that the
validator doesn't recognise. injectIntoHtml only stripped <title>, so
every prerendered page inherited those tags, producing 10,426 critical
issues (duplicate canonicals, over-length descriptions, unknown JSON-LD
types). The build was kept passing only by SEO_GATE_BYPASS=1.

Changes:
- vite-plugin-prerender.ts: injectIntoHtml now also strips
  <meta name="description|keywords|robots">, <link rel="canonical">,
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang>, all og:*/twitter:* meta and every
  <script type="application/ld+json"> from the base HTML before
  injecting the route-specific headMeta. Verified via a unit-style
  regex check against index.html that no leak vectors remain.
- vite-plugin-seo-validate.ts: removed the SEO_GATE_BYPASS and
  SEO_ISSUES_THRESHOLD env-var escape hatches. The validator now
  unconditionally throws on any critical issue, missing trust file or
  score < 50.

Verification: confirmed CI workflows (bundle-size-gate.yml,
deploy-now.yml, lc-governance-tests.yml) never set the bypass, so
removing it is safe. End-to-end `vite build` could not complete in this
environment because the long-running build process was repeatedly
killed before reaching the seo-validate step; the strip logic was
unit-tested directly against index.html instead.

Follow-ups proposed: generate sitemap.xml at build time, add RSS/Atom
feeds, and reduce build duration / circular chunks.

